# Pontia documentation

Pontia turns your device into an agent cloud. Coding agents run with the tools and project files on your device while you monitor and control their Sessions through the hosted Remote Dashboard. A local Dashboard is also available for direct access to `pontiad`.

## Start here

- [Getting started](/docs/getting-started) — install Pontia and prepare your Agent Clients.
- [Initialization](/docs/initialization) — use the interactive wizard or initialize step by step with non-interactive commands.
- [Remote access](/docs/remote-access) — register a device and connect through the hosted Dashboard.
- [Dashboard guide](/docs/dashboard) — activate a Workspace, start a Session, and control agent work.
- [How Pontia works](/docs/how-it-works) — understand local execution and the boundaries between your device, Pontia Cloud, and Edge.

## Remote access and security

- [Device and account management](/docs/device-management) — rename, rotate, remove, and revoke remote access resources.
- [Self-host an Edge](/docs/self-hosted-edge) — deploy and operate an encrypted relay on a public Linux server.
- [Security](/docs/security) — review trust boundaries, E2E encryption, credentials, and incident response.

## Use Pontia

- [Agent Clients](/docs/agent-clients) — configure pi and Codex and understand their capability differences.
- [Workspaces](/docs/workspaces) — configure project directories and file discovery.
- [Workflows](/docs/workflows) — run durable, staged agent work with explicit Handoffs and replanning.

## Reference

- [Configuration](/docs/configuration) and [CLI reference](/docs/cli)
- [Updating Pontia](/docs/updating)
- Platform notes for [Linux](/docs/platforms/linux) and [macOS](/docs/platforms/macos)
- [Troubleshooting](/docs/troubleshooting) and [FAQ](/docs/faq)

Agent execution stays on your device. Remote Dashboard traffic is encrypted end to end between the browser and device; an Edge provides connectivity without receiving the plaintext business traffic.
